60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, since the window is impossible, C is out. @Rin, B might be unfair to the small house. @Servas, A costs a lot. What do you think?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I agree C is too harsh. @Rin, B feels heavy for the small home. @Servas, A seems best, if we can share the cost kindly.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, C is infeasible. @Rin, B ignores the ninety-centimetre frontage. @Servas, A’s four-month timeline and cost burden are the only remaining variables to weigh.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, C is out! @Shizue, A is nice, but it stays at one gate! @Asuka, B is fair, but the tiny house can’t fit it!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Shizue"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, you are right; A leaves the burden at one gate. @Kenji, C is impossible. @Shizue, B is the only path to true equality, despite the small frontage.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Kenji"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, wait! If B moves the bins, the tiny house doesn’t have to hold them forever. That fixes the fairness issue. @Rin, does that sound better?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, yes, moving it shares the burden. But @Rin, can the tiny house even fit it? We must be kind to their space.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, B is logical. The rotation distributes the burden, avoiding the single-point failure of A. @Rin, the ninety-centimetre frontage is a constraint, but not a disqualifier if the rotation is strict.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, yes! If it moves, nobody is stuck forever! But @Shizue, what if the tiny house can’t fit it? We need a rule for that!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, a strict rotation is just. @Shizue, kindness means sharing the load, not avoiding it. @Kenji, B preserves our peace.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Shizue"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I agree! If it moves, nobody is stuck forever. @Servas, B keeps us talking. @Asuka, the rotation is fair. I vote B.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Servas"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I agree. B shares the burden gently. @Rin, let us trust the rotation to be fair. I vote B.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, B is the only option that distributes the burden logically. A fails on cost and fairness; C is infeasible. I vote B.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, I agree! Moving it means nobody is stuck forever. It’s fair and fun! I vote B!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, B honors our shared lane and our differing needs. It is the path to lasting peace. I vote B.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"B wins! We can still be friends. @Rin, high five! @Servas, thank you for guiding us. Let’s keep the lane peaceful.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I am so glad we found a way to share this gently. @Rin, your bright eyes helped us see the truth. Let us keep our smiles and our peace.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, B is adopted. The rotation eliminates the single-point failure. We must now define the strict intervals to ensure the burden is distributed equally.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, high five! Yay! @Asuka, I hope the tiny house gets a break. Let’s keep our lane happy and clean!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, a high five is well earned. @Asuka, let us draft those intervals with care. May this rotation bring lasting harmony to our lane.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
